<div class="intro"><aside class="profile"><img class="portrait" src="/assets/portrait.jpg" alt="Shanshan Xu"><div class="contacts"><details open><summary>📩 Email</summary><p>{firstname.lastname} at di.ku.dk</p></details><p>📎 <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shanshan-xu33/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></p><p>🎓 <a href="https://scholar.google.de/citations?user=dSDjjCEAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a></p><p>🦋 <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/sxu3.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bsky</a></p></div></aside><div class="bio"><h2>I’m a Postdoctoral Researcher in NLP at the University of Copenhagen. I completed my PhD in LegalNLP <a href="https://www.cs.cit.tum.de/lt/home/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">at TU Munich</a>, supervised by <a href="https://www.cs.cit.tum.de/lt/team/matthias-grabmair/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matthias Grabmair</a>, and mentored by <a href="https://bplank.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Barbara Plank</a>. My research interest is Human-Centered AI , Legal NLP and Technical AI Governance.</h2><h3>I initiated and organized <a href="https://pandora-workshop.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PANDORA</a>, a workshop @ EMNLP 2026 focused on pluralistic alignment and sociotechnical AI evaluation. I am also part of the organizing committee of the Natural Legal Language Processing (<a href="https://sites.google.com/view/nllp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NLLP</a>) workshop.</h3></div></div>
